[Themes "d4-pawn-centre,isolated-pawn"]

1. e4 c5 2. c3 d5
3. exd5 { Takes the pawn rather than let Black capture on e4. Black has to recapture with the queen or the knight. }
3... Qxd5
4. d4 { Claims the centre and prepares to hit the queen with developing moves, so White can gain time. }
4... Nf6
5. Nf3 { Develops and defends d4. White now has a lead in development because the queen is out early. }
5... Bg4
(5... Nc6 6. Be3 e6 7. Na3)
(5... e6 6. Na3)
6. Be2 { Develops and prepares to castle. The bishop also defends the knight on f3, which the black bishop pins. }
6... e6
7. h3 { Asks the bishop on g4 a question. Taking on f3 gives White the two bishops. }
7... Bh5
8. O-O { Gets the king safe before the centre opens. } 8... Nc6
9. Be3 { Develops the last minor piece and guards d4, which Black is about to capture on. }
9... cxd4
10. cxd4 { Recaptures with the pawn to rebuild the centre. } 10... Be7
11. Nc3 { The knight attacks the queen, so White gains a tempo. }
11... Qd6
12. Qb3 *
